# WARNING / ONE TILT / WARNING / TWO TILTS (task 18) -- ordinary gameplay, no
# sleic.c probe.  The factory-default tilt-warnings adjustment (NVRAM 0x42) is 1,
# giving a zero-warning budget ([4134:0033] = NVRAM[0x42]-1, reloaded at every
# ball start, sub_D9EBB) -- the first TILT press already fully tilts with no
# WARNING screen at all (matches the committed en/ corpus, which presses TILT once
# and marks it "full-tilt" straight away).  To see the two warning screens for
# real, the NVRAM's own tilt-warnings byte has to be 3 (budget 2) BEFORE this
# script runs -- there is no live DIP for it, only the TECHNICAL > TILTS service
# menu record (F14) or a direct NVRAM edit:
#
#   python3 -c "
#   import sys
#   p = sys.argv[1]
#   d = bytearray(open(p,'rb').read())
#   d[0x42] = 3
#   open(p,'wb').write(d)" <nvram_directory>/iomoont.nv
#
# applied to an ALREADY-BOOTED once .nv (a brand new file is all zero and the
# firmware's own signature check would just rewrite it back to the factory 1 --
# boot once with no key script, quit, patch, then run this script against that
# same nvram_directory without wiping it.  Keys: KEYCODE_1 START, KEYCODE_5 COIN,
# KEYCODE_T TILT (src/wpc/sims/sleic/iomoon.c, simulation.txt).
    40 mark boot
   200 mark credit
   200 tap 8 KEYCODE_5
   260 mark ball-1-start
   260 tap 8 KEYCODE_1
   500 mark tilt-1
   500 tap 10 KEYCODE_T
   900 mark tilt-2
   900 tap 10 KEYCODE_T
  1200 mark settle
  1400 quit
